From 121fc9c5566ab89a3d19916f7c5cd25cf6316015 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nezumi-ai-kmp <kmp@nezumi.local>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 04:39:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(shared): use preparePost().execute + single cached
 channel for streaming

Root cause of infinite loop / stuck first response: engines used http.post()
(buffers full body) and readStreamLine() called response.bodyAsChannel() on every
line, which returns a fresh channel positioned at the start -> the same first
NDJSON/SSE line was re-read forever, so done:true / [DONE] was never reached and
the tool-call loop never ran.

Fix: switch all 5 engines to preparePost(...).execute { response -> ... } and read
lines from a single cached ByteReadChannel (withStreamChannel) so reading actually
advances through the stream. Ollama 'done' now read via booleanOrNull and tool_calls
only synthesized on the final (done) chunk.
